        "id": 19660,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-01-06T20:32:53.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Principle of the Indestructible says, \"During Roleplaying: You ignore damage from unpowered close-combat weapons and attacks, such as clubs and non-powered fists, or basic ranged attacks, such as slings and arrows.\"&nbsp; Unlike every other Principle, this one appears to have an application that's not just \"during roleplay,\" but during combat as well.&nbsp; Is that the intent?&nbsp; Or do clubs and arrows somehow only hurt you only when it's not an action scene?</p>\n<p>Dive &amp; Drop says, in part, \"Whatever that minion rolls as defense Attacks another target of your choice.\"&nbsp; The language is weird because it's not the hero attacking, it's not the minion attacking, it's the&nbsp;<em>roll</em>&nbsp;that's attacking.&nbsp; What/whose modifiers apply?&nbsp; Would it matter if there was a floating \"all hero attacks\" or \"all enemy attacks\" modifier in place?&nbsp; Also, if you have an ability that triggers on you defeating an enemy or an enemy attacking, can either of those be triggered?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:53:25.559Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 41,
